I'm quite surprised nobody has mentioned this : Peaceful giants do not
move boulders. In fact friendly giants must be one of the least
troublesome monsters to be generated in Sokoban as they can move past
boulders (and consequently they won't get trapped in your way).

So, what should you have done? Not killed him. What if there was a
hostile giant? Well, I don't think I've ever seen one in Sokoban so
you must've been fairly high level and/or unlucky. Kill them ASAP if
they do show up. If their dropped boulder gets in the way, smash it.

As to the general question of what to do if Sokoban gets broken : just
suck up the luck penalty and break the boulders with a pick-axe. I
usually do at least to minetown before Sokoban so I nearly always have
a pick-axe by then. If you don't have one, slip through with care if
you like, or go do more of the mines until you get one (or some other
means). And if you end up in a precarious situation like being hugged
by an owlbear with no inventory then engraving Elbereth in the dust
until it lets go then moving away is probably a safer bet than trying
to punch it to death.

